<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Description">Description</span></h2>
<p>When toggling the Render Lightmaps and Wait option's Run? status to no a warning pops up that "you are trying to toggle the enabled status of a mandatory or prohibited operation."
</p><p>However, the Render Lightmaps and Wait option is neither Mandatory or Prohibited but merely Recommended. Therefore either its Required? status is incorrect (i.e. it should be Mandatory); the Warning message text is incorrect (i.e. it should read "a Recommended or Prohibited") or the alert is triggering incorrectly.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Workarounds">Workarounds</span></h2>
<p>The warning message allows you to carry on and toggle the run status anyway, it just requires a second click-through.
</p>
